From 16c4573ef1f441cf689742919e283614aa243856 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tillmann Severin <tillmann.severin@mailbox.org>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:46:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 43/49] media: histb-demux: present the demultiplexer to the
 DVB core

With the whole multiplex arriving by direct memory access, what is
left is to hand it over.  Each filled block holds a whole number of
packets, so it goes straight to the software filters, and is then
returned to the free queue: without that last step the capture stops
dead once the ring has been through once.

The adapter belongs here rather than in the front end driver, which
only ever registered one because there was nothing else to attach to.
It is now found through a phandle from the board description, and the
front end is registered on the demultiplexer's own adapter, so the
two appear as one device as they should.

Blocks are collected by a polling worker for the moment.  The
hardware can raise an interrupt when a block is finished, which will
be better, but polling keeps the first working version simple.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
